In-Reply-To: <n9g4k9jVh3A.Jc1iQZ1rwaoJ@davis-rug.groups.google.com>
References: <n9g4k9jVh3A.Jc1iQZ1rwaoJ@davis-rug.groups.google.com>
Archived-At: <https://groups.google.com/g/davis-rug/c/n9g4k9jVh3A/m/-_WpKSK1vlAJ>
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset="utf-8"
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

I think it should have been translated as "units", rather than "metric". The function returns Euclidean distance, the relevant part is pasted below, which will be in the units in which the points are specified.

        d = outer(x[, 1], y[, 1], "-")^2
        if (ncol(x) > 2)
            for (i in 2:ncol(x)) d = d + outer(x[, i], y[, i],
                "-")^2
        matrix(sqrt(d), nrow(x), nrow(y))

