Since some of the advice already is general programming knowledge, one item I tend to add for new programmers is that trying to read code from others is a great way to learn and gain a sense for appropriate style, functions, and conventions. It's how I picked up Python quickly, and my lack of doing it is likely a large reason that I'm terrible in R.

Also, as an addon to Vince's comment about versioning, there is a free online book called Version Control by Example that goes through using a few different version control systems - http://www.ericsink.com/vcbe/html/index.html - you can probably read it in part of an afternoon, since it's short, if you have an idea of which system you want to use.

-Nick

